codex
Lane B4 complete. Summary of what changed, then the verbatim evidence.

## Files written (allowed set only)
| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `packaging/public-plugin/plugin.json` | **Rewritten as the official Agent Plugins 1.0 root manifest**: `$schema` = vendor `$id`, `name: pipd-ls-sp-public-skills` (matches the vendor pattern), `version/description/repository/license/keywords`, `extensions["com.pipd.s4"]` (PIPD bookkeeping, verbatim) + `extensions["com.openai"].interface`. No top-level private keys. |
| `packaging/public-plugin/plugin.release.json` | **New** — PIPD release bookkeeping (claim ceiling, portal state, publisher record, icon digests, the eight skill names, pinned vendor digest), still shaped to the closed key set of the untouched `plugin.schema.json` subset. |
| `packaging/public-plugin/vendor-plugin.schema.json` | **New** — byte copy of the round's downloaded schema: 1805 bytes, sha256 `0a4aad95…ab883`. |
| `tools/build_public_plugin.py` | Vendor-schema lock + two-manifest gates; `validate_subset` now also honours object-form `additionalProperties`; receipt records `official_schema_sha256`/`official_schema_id`. |
| `tests/test_public_plugin_packaging.py` | Extended 19 → 28 cases (fixtures retargeted to the official manifest + release doc; historical cases preserved). |
| `docs/adr/ADR-0001-public-plugin-manifest-and-derivation.md` | **New**, 50 lines, records (i)–(iv). |

New builder gates: `VENDOR_SCHEMA_MISSING/INVALID/ID_MISMATCH`, `OFFICIAL_SCHEMA_ID_MISMATCH`, `VENDOR_SCHEMA_DIGEST_MISMATCH`, `RELEASE_BOOKKEEPING_MISSING`, `RELEASE_EXTENSION_MISMATCH`. Owner-gate order unchanged (derivation → digest → publisher → icon); `MANIFEST_SCHEMA_VIOLATION` and `ICON_*` codes retained. The old `OFFICIAL_SCHEMA_DIGEST_MISMATCH` is subsumed: the pinned digest now names the official vendor schema bytes (disclosed in the module docstring and ADR, together with the untouched-subset description residual).

The real checked-in candidate passes all manifest/vendor/extension gates and still fails closed at the first owner gate, writing nothing: `REFUSED OWNER_INPUT_MISSING: no owner derivation record for skill 'pipd-assurance-tqaep' …`

## 1. `python -m unittest tests.test_public_plugin_packaging -v`
```
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Ran 28 tests in 1.438s

OK
```

## 2. `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`
```
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Ran 569 tests in 111.535s

OK (skipped=6)
```

## 3. Exact refusal string for a vendor schema digest mismatch
```
REFUSED VENDOR_SCHEMA_DIGEST_MISMATCH: pinned official_schema_sha256 aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa does not match the vendor schema bytes it validates against (0a4aad95ce337878ad38802ebf0daa3fde76abe3f65400c86bcbb1ec0b3ab883)
```
Code: `VENDOR_SCHEMA_DIGEST_MISMATCH` (conformance code unchanged; only the pin moves from the local subset to the locked vendor bytes).
